    tail: [decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.remote_build", decl_name: "remote_build_host_pin")],
  },
  question: "When work-exec-2's durable route replaces the SSH transport, does host choice move to select_supply with the remote build's request as the demand, and is anything of the roster walk and the pin kept? Until then the walk and the pin are the admitted scaffold of gunbc.design_ruling::remote_build_ssh_dispatch_is_an_admitted_scaffold, and no selection policy is added to them.",
  sightings: FreeSemigroup {
    head: ConcernSighting {
      revision: "7711690f3f55ae40d41fbee3fc856e13b65c3c95",
      evidence: FreeSemigroup {
        head: CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.remote_build", decl_name: "remote_build_next_step") },
        tail: [CitesDeclaration { declaration: decl_ref(module_path: "product.fabric.selection", decl_name: "select_supply") }],
      },
      account: "Read at this revision: remote_build_next_step folds over the dispatch roster in order and remote_build_host_pin narrows it to one host; no module under dag/gunbc/compute imports product.fabric.selection, gunbc.fabric.fabric_control_plane or gunbc.fabric.fabric_executor_class (git grep over dag/gunbc/compute). The remote_build module header states the divergence with its reason.",
    },
    tail: [],
  },
  disposition: Triaged {
    home: ExistingHome { model: decl_ref(module_path: "product.fabric.selection", decl_name: "select_supply") },
    preserve: [
      PreservedObligation {
        holder: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.remote_build", decl_name: "remote_build_next_step"),
        control: Present { value: decl_ref(module_path: "gunbc.compute.remote_build", decl_name: "remote_build_next_step") },
        statement: "until the durable route lands, a pin to a host off the dispatch roster stays a refusal and never widens to the roster",
